      ("Replacement", "Replace Every 10 Years", ["Smoke alarms must be replaced every 10 years. If your alarms are older than that, are ionisation types or are not interconnected, they need upgrading under Queensland rules, and we can replace them for you.", "Many Sunshine Coast homes still have old ionisation alarms. As a guide, a 10-year lithium photoelectric alarm typically costs around $120 to $180 installed, and a typical three-bedroom home needs four to six alarms."], [], [W+"2025/11/Sm-Alarms-4.jpg"]),
